From 0b41148f8871e4d314a49544b400481cf9545459 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:09:41 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] dsv41: TF_DS_ENGRAM_METRICS times every read of Engram's
 table rows and publishes tensorfold:engram_lookup_seconds on /metrics (on by
 default)

Engram's rows are read from the tables on the host before an Engram layer's projection: a decode round reads
~70 random 4 KiB rows a stream, and a cold prompt reads 2 x 12 x 2,048 rows a chunk (~0.07 s by AIO where the
pool's preads take ~0.5 s on one GB10). That I/O is where a slow disk or a table copy shows up, and /metrics had
no sign of it: --profile's engram_read_ms is a per-round average printed at exit, and the per-request fields
carry no split.

The timing is on by default; TF_DS_ENGRAM_METRICS=0 turns it off, as TF_DS_LOAD_PREFETCH's 0 does (every other
value and unset leave it on). Each read of the tables is timed (the pool's gather or the AIO batch's
submit-and-wait) into an atomic histogram in the Engram host: a decode round's, a prompt chunk's read-ahead, and
TF_DS_ENGRAM_LEAD's reader threads. The lane host copies it on its engine thread (as it does the cache and KV
counters), Status.engram carries it, and /metrics renders tensorfold:engram_lookup_seconds (buckets 1 ms .. 10 s,
+Inf past 10 s) with _sum and _count. With TF_DS_ENGRAM_METRICS=0: no clock read, no metric, every path as before.

The histogram covers this rank's reads (rank 0's, the one serving /metrics): the ranks split the hash columns,
so each reads its own half. --profile's prefill split (pstamp synchronizes the stream) is now gated on its own
flag so the timing alone does not slow a prompt pass.

Also fixes 0051's decodeLaunches test calls for 0053's `places` argument: the dsv41 module's host tests did not
compile after both patches, so this patch's tests could not run.

Not served on a pair yet: host tests only (no pair had the metric on). The timing's own cost is two clock reads a
table read, against an I/O of milliseconds.

Tests: prompt.zig (the switch's values; the buckets and the sum, past every edge), metrics.zig (the histogram
present with the stats, absent without), zig/tests/server/zig_test.sh (177 pass), zig build test (487/488, the
one failure lane_host's prefill-interleave test, which fails the same way on the unpatched series and passes on a
rerun).
